The pylint fragments are called out explicitly because pylint is copyleft while this
repository is not. What appears here is diff context around edits of a few lines each;
no pylint file is reproduced whole and nothing here is runnable as pylint. It is quotation
in a research artifact, not redistribution of the program. If the pylint maintainers
disagree, contact the author and those ten records will be removed.

This follows the practice of SWE-bench's own experiments repository, which publishes
per-instance patches, trajectories and execution logs against these same projects.

